{
  "comment": "Exploration domains only. NOVA expands each one with current Google Trends, related searches, public-web evidence and CJ supplier availability, then scores what it finds. A seed is never itself a recommendation - it only decides where NOVA is allowed to look. Breadth here directly determines breadth of the catalogue, so this list is deliberately cross-category. Products failing the margin, competition, return-risk or repeat-purchase gates are rejected regardless of which seed produced them.",
  "seedNotes": {
    "regulated": "Supplements, medicines, medical devices and cosmetics making health claims are deliberately absent. NOVA's analyst flags these as regulated and rejects them, so seeding them only burns API calls.",
    "highReturn": "Apparel and footwear are absent because sizing drives a return rate no margin survives. Size-free fashion accessories are included instead.",
    "seasonal": "Indian festive seeds are included on purpose. Diwali, Rakhi and wedding season are the largest demand spikes in this market, and NOVA's seasonality signal can only detect them if it looks."
  },
